@* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Site/AccessIsDenied.aspx (+ .aspx.cs) -> Components/Pages/Site/AccessIsDenied.razor
   (checklist task 93).

   MasterPageFile="~/BackendMaster.Master" -> @layout BackendLayout. The Script/StyleSheet/
   BottomScript <asp:Content> blocks were all EMPTY -> no <SectionContent>.

   Page_Init built the body programmatically into Placeholder1:
       h1 = Warnings.AccessIsDenied -> HtmlControlHelper.GetDivider() -> p = Warnings.NotAuthorized
   That exact markup lives in Specialist 4's Components/Base/AccessIsDeniedContent.razor, which
   AuthorizationOutlet renders IN PLACE for the former Server.Transfer call sites. It is REUSED
   here rather than duplicated, so the in-place denial and this routed page can never drift apart.

   The cookie scheme's AccessDeniedPath (Program.cs) is this route, so it must keep it verbatim.
   --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- *@
@page "/Site/AccessIsDenied"
@layout BackendLayout
@inherits MixERPAuthorizedPageBase

<AccessIsDeniedContent />

@code {
    /// <summary>
    ///     Page_Init: <c>this.IsLandingPage = true</c> -- the denial page has no menu entry of its
    ///     own, so the policy check must not run against it (and must certainly not redirect a
    ///     denied user back to a denial page). Set in the constructor because the base activation
    ///     sequence that reads it runs in OnInitializedAsync.
    /// </summary>
    public AccessIsDenied()
    {
        this.IsLandingPage = true;
    }
}
